WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:09.710
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:20.340
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.460
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:06.910
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:14.210
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:20.890
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:28.040
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.700
Making another unauthorized
flight, Chor Tempest?

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.740
Vura!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.500
Dux Guragief ordered us to go
on a special training mission.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:51.280
You’re all busy with
regular duties, right?

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:56.410
Yeah, we’re tired. Night patrol requires
far more vigilance than day patrol.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.960
And enemy encounters are likelier.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.420
It’s easier to just float
around during the day.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.850
But your chor used to do
nothing but daytime patrol.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.070
The night shift was always our job.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.940
But that’s not the case now.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.960
The top chor on
Arcus Prima is now us, Rubor.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.030
If you don’t like it,
then prove you’re still worthy.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.040
Step aside. We’re exhausted.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.540
Everyone, let them pass.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.080
By the way, which Ri Majon?

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:40.890
The Dandelion Ri Majon.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.340
Dandelion?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.520
The ceremonial Ri Majon
used for diplomatic purposes.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.640
Why use
an old-fashioned Ri Majon like that?

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.810
Vura!

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.190
Help yourself to
the leftover candy on my desk!

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.240
Don’t wake me coming back!

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:07.200
<b>Over International Waters</b>

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.100
Wow!
Look how spotless you are now.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.820
These kids worked hard.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:41.360
It’s quite an antique,
so they had a rough time.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.510
Thanks.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.330
My grandpa flew this
when he was young.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.360
Your grandfather
was a Simoun sibylla too?

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:55.880
So after he went to the Spring and
stopped flying, he still treasured this.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:25.240
They’re jealous that we always
used to be assigned night patrol.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:30.500
When Chor Rubor used to run into
Neviril, they’d just look on from afar.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.740
Be proud of yourselves.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:39.610
As a member of Chor Tempest, I plan
to take this chor right back to the top.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:45.630
Right. As far as wanting to see
Tempest back on top, I’m with her.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.830
Well, I guess you’re right.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:51.890
Since we won’t have to go to the
Spring as long as we keep winning?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.520
Well, I can’t wait to go.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:57.220
Then what’s stopping you?

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.030
I want to go with
the person I care about.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:05.170
Then when I emerge from
the Spring, I’ll be a man.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.240
And she’ll be a woman…

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.120
And you’ll consummate
things then and there?

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.000
Quiet down.

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:16.710
Listen up, everybody.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:21.380
There are two obstacles
to becoming the best chor.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.920
Unless we get two new members…

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.930
…we won’t be able
to fly six Simouns at once.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.180
What’s the other thing?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.680
Neviril…

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.440
If Neviril and Aer flew as a pair…

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:39.190
…it wouldn’t be a stretch
to see our chor back on top!

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.650
Para-sama…

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.600
…you’re giving up on Neviril?

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:51.210
Let’s do it in front of the Arcus Prima!
So that the dux and Neviril can see.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.930
Morinas-san, higher!

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.850
Am I not good enough
for Sibylla Aurea?

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.520
Morinas-san, please concentrate!

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.560
Okay, okay.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.380
You have to lead the others.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:19.560
Right.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.850
So who’s this loved one?

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:25.360
Floe, I’m hearing bad
things about you lately.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.690
No way! It’s not true, is it, Alty?

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.360
Of course it’s true.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.060
I’m so happy…

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.160
Para-sama,
you’re responding to my feelings.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.300
What are you talking about?

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.870
I was sure you hated me.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.770
Since the other day…

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.840
Be specific!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.290
Huh?

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:58.350
Arcus Niger? We’re not
supposed to rendezvous till later.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.810
That’s the Niger. No mistake.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.460
An emergency, perhaps?

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.590
I’m sure they’re just being
rushed by the higher-ups.

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:11.570
You should summon
the Tempest girls back.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.980
Arcus Niger!

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:18.830
Niger?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.560
They’re supposed to be west
of the great temple… Why…

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.930
A Simile Simoun!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.430
A messenger?

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:40.480
Even so…

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.730
How lame is that pilot?
Missing the cable like that!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.780
No, they’re avoiding it on purpose.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.000
Hey!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.910
Hey!

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.540
Talk!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.040
You’re supposed to be Chor Tempest?

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:01.250
Since the Plumbum highlands and
our nation share similar customs…

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.980
…I didn’t think the decor
here would offend you.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.440
Let’s have
Tempus Spatium be scarce.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:12.530
That would undermine
our authority severely…

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.950
The highlanders worship
a deity named Animus.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.820
Historically speaking…

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.310
…Animus and Tempus Spatium
are in fact the same god.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:26.210
The highlands and Kyuukoku
do not acknowledge this.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:29.730
It’s best to avoid
unnecessary stimulation?

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:32.210
For the sake of peace.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.920
Tempus Spatium would
be glad to be concealed.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.500
Peace conference?

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:14.340
Right. It’s fair to say we’re battling
all our neighboring countries.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.970
Each one,
because of economic strife…

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:20.220
They want the Simouns.
No matter what.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.260
Right.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:25.890
To be more precise,
they’re after the helical motors.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.730
Unearthed only from ruins,
the wings that give Simouns flight.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:35.630
But now the Plumbum highlands
have come to broker a peace deal.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:39.240
It’s been decided the first conference
will be held in international waters.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:43.310
In utmost secrecy of course.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:46.500
So they’ll hold this conference
on the Arcus Prima, huh?

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:51.500
Who cares about politics?
Are we free to use the maju pool?

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.670
I think they’ll say not
to act without permission.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.510
Hey, it’s them.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.760
The ones flying that Simile before.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:03.010
Why are they
wandering around here?

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.340
They’re headed this way.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:17.710
Why are they on our ship?

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:21.610
The most obvious reason is
that they’re new members…

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:27.950
Hey, I bet she’ll say something like,
“Chor Tempest sure is a letdown.”

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.710
Right, right.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:36.670
Sorry for earlier,
members of Chor Tempest.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.840
So it was you two after all.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.720
Still, you sure are a letdown.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:58.530
Is it that funny, my lady Roatreamon?

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.690
I don’t blame you
for not remembering.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:07.930
I just lived on your estate…

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:11.040
…as the daughter of two
of your many servants.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.150
Come now, Mamina.

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.070
Mamina?

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:49.390
I am honored that
you remember me, my lady.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.580
As of today,
I’ve been ordered to transfer…

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.980
…from Arcus Niger’s
Chor Ignus to Chor Tempest.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:05.050
I’m Sibylla Mamina. I’m pleased
to make your acquaintance.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:09.810
And I’m Yun.
I’m also joining Chor Tempest.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:13.520
I have one thing to say. I despise war.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.380
That’s all.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:22.870
Somebody!
Somebody, please help us!

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.030
Sibylla Aurea’s room…

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.410
What’s this about Neviril?

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:40.380
Neviril!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.880
Paraietta…

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:47.020
What’s going on?
What do you think you’re doing?

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:49.900
Sibylla Aurea sleeps
alone in her room.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:52.890
That’s a privilege
granted to her alone! Hey!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:55.140
Starting today,
she’s sharing her room.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.350
Father!

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.860
Para, it’s been a while.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:03.510
Yes, it has, Vice Chancellor.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:09.110
Neviril, I think this is a good way to
immediately bond with your new pair.

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.240
New pair?

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.490
Then that’s my bed.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.500
A “new pair”…Father.

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:20.500
Yes, I’m assigning Mamina.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.460
Mamina?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.500
Excuse me.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:37.350
Pairs should be formed out of mutual
need and according to the natural flow.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:42.350
You were once a sibylla, Father,
so you should be well aware of that.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:47.330
Neviril, in this day and age,
it doesn’t work that way anymore.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:52.800
You must take this step now
or your name will be tarnished.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:56.390
I was an auriga,
but if I can pair with you…

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.040
…I’d be happy to fly as a sagitta.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:05.470
Mamina is not from
a family befitting a sibylla.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:10.980
But of all the great temple’s
candidates, she scored the highest.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:14.180
As far as the Wave Crest
and Tsunami Ri Majons…

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.560
…I can pray better than anyone.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.350
Those are all highly dangerous.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:23.360
Which enable us to annihilate
more enemies in one blow.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.500
All I want is for you to snap out of it.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:28.690
Granted, a tragedy occurred.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:35.120
But you shall overcome that and
regain your glory as Sibylla Aurea.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:40.060
Meaning that your standing in
the council will be safe, Father?

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:44.400
I don’t understand what’s
going on in your head, Neviril.

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.630
If you’re put off by battle,
then you should go to the Spring.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:51.410
You’ll surely become a lovely woman.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:57.380
But if you’re put off by the Spring and
refuse to fly a Simoun, what then?

00:15:57.380 --> 00:16:00.640
You’re telling me
to give you an answer.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.150
You’re old enough now.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.150
Is Neviril coming back?

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.780
Hey, Aer, you should
pair with me after all.

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:13.590
I like Neviril.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.160
Neviril really is popular.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.140
I think I’ll give up on her.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.620
What will you do?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:27.920
I’ll pair with someone. But even so,
I’ll still despise what we do.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.880
If so, then just hurry on to the Spring.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.130
I couldn’t do that!

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.700
Already, many of my friends,
despite being priestesses…

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:43.530
…were sent to the battlefield since
they could fly Simouns and perished.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:47.650
I couldn’t run away
from that just on my own!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:50.400
That reason sounds like a death wish.

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:00.910
Paraietta.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:06.260
I always thought you and Neviril
would fly as a pair one day.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:07.670
Vice Chancellor…

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:11.170
No matter what, I will protect Neviril.

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:55.420
Mamina, I’m sorry.

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:56.590
I’m still…

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:05.640
Sibylla Aurea,
I want you to be my pair…

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:08.560
…body and soul.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:15.400
Sibylla Mamina, even if you
take my body by force…

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:18.320
…you will never be my pair.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:21.300
Neviril, try to understand.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:25.660
I’ve got to pair up with you,
no matter what it takes.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.510
Aer!

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:57.320
You actually used that rope
to come through the window?

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.820
You’re such a funny girl.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:09.090
All six Simouns will be needed
for the Dandelion Ri Majon.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:11.330
As Chor Tempest is now…

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:15.380
We’ve already bolstered the ranks.
Is that not enough?

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:19.060
It’s about whether it can be
done with those new members.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:23.500
It’s a prayer for a key event, the
peace conference with the highlands.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:26.350
We cannot risk failure of any kind.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:31.300
All I’m asking for is a Ri Majon
performed by Chor Tempest.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.130
If you cannot comply
with my request…

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.360
What will you do?

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:41.880
I don’t want my daughter
to suffer any more humiliation.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:44.410
I don’t want her to get hurt.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:05.570
Mamina! You want to challenge
me in the maju pool too?

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.400
Challenge you?

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:10.140
To decide who’ll pair up with Neviril.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.020
It’s not a matter of challenging you.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:20.030
What are you doing?

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:22.930
As long as we have these outfits on…

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:27.490
…the helical motors activate, allowing
us to float! But if it’s removed…

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:28.670
You crazy?

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:30.470
Say you’ll give up on her!

00:20:30.470 --> 00:20:32.250
Cut it out!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.240
I’m going to pair with her!

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:37.000
Same for me! But that’s up to her!

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:41.610
You’re of low birth and only made it
here because you can fly a Simoun!

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:44.210
One such as you is unworthy of her!

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:46.510
The same goes for you too!

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:55.410
Let go of me!

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:57.410
Aer!

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:06.530
As long as such breaches
of conduct continue…

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:10.240
…we can only conclude
Chor Tempest no longer functions.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.760
By that, do you mean…

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:18.070
Once the peace conference
is over, I want Chor Tempest…

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:21.140
…to disband.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:23.550
Please wait, Vice Chancellor!

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.960
Then what of your daughter?

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.530
That’s the point.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:33.430
I can’t leave her in this chor. She’ll go
to the Spring before she’s hurt further.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:36.480
U-Um, then what about me?

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:39.150
You’ve disappointed me.

00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:47.830
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:52.070
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:59.110
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:06.670
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:19.630
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.630 --> 00:23:24.800
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:28.810
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.810 --> 00:23:32.820
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:38.140
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:44.220
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:47.660
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:53.330
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:59.700
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:08.210
The highland priestess named Anglas…

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:12.430
…will be staying with
Chor Tempest for the time being.

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:16.950
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>Prayer</b>

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:18.320
Prayer.
